{"name":"Three Swords","status":"ok","title":"Three Swords","pageId":91204,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\">\n\n\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Three Swords</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-map_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-map-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Settlement</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eastern_Shaar\" title=\"Eastern Shaar\">Eastern Shaar</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/South_Faer%C3%BBn\" title=\"South Faerûn\">south Faerûn</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Commerce<sup id=\"cite_ref-ESA-66_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-ESA-66-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-ESp52-3_3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-ESp52-3-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"exports\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Exports</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Food and drink.</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">History<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-120,121_4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-120,121-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"disestablished\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Disestablished</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/1385_DR\" title=\"1385 DR\">1385 DR</a> (destroyed)</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Three Swords</b> was a fortified town on the upper side of the <a href=\"/wiki/Landrise\" title=\"Landrise\">Landrise</a> in the <a href=\"/wiki/Eastern_Shaar\" title=\"Eastern Shaar\">Eastern Shaar</a>, <i>circa</i> the <a href=\"/wiki/1373_DR\" title=\"1373 DR\">Year of Rogue Dragons, 1373 DR</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-map_1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-map-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-157_5-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-157-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> It was destroyed as a result of the <a href=\"/wiki/Spellplague\" title=\"Spellplague\">Spellplague</a> in the <a href=\"/wiki/1385_DR\" title=\"1385 DR\">Year of Blue Fire, 1385 DR</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-120,121_4-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-120,121-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Geography\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geography</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Trade\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Trade</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Defenses\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Defenses</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geography\">Geography</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Geography\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Three_Swords?veaction=edit&section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Geography\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three Swords was located on the <a href=\"/wiki/Trader%27s_Way\" title=\"Trader's Way\">Trader's Way</a> between <a href=\"/wiki/Channathgate\" title=\"Channathgate\">Channathgate</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Eartheart\" title=\"Eartheart\">Eartheart</a> where the road scaled the <a href=\"/wiki/Landrise\" title=\"Landrise\">Landrise</a>. It was approximately 200 miles (320 kilometers) east of Channathgate and 150 miles (240 kilometers) west of Eartheart.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-map_1-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-map-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-157_5-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-157-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trade\">Trade</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Trade\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Three_Swords?veaction=edit&section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Trade\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three Swords did brisk business with <a href=\"/wiki/Kh%C3%B4ltar\" title=\"Khôltar\">Khôltar</a> which was hungry for food and drink, especially the potent spirit <a href=\"/wiki/Amberfire\" title=\"Amberfire\">amberfire</a> that originated in Three Swords.<sup id=\"cite_ref-ESA-66_2-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-ESA-66-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-ESp52-3_3-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-ESp52-3-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Defenses\">Defenses</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Defenses\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Three_Swords?veaction=edit&section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Defenses\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The town was surrounded by walls and benefited from regular patrols of the Trader's Way and the Landrise by the <span class=\"new\" title=\"Steel Shields (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvU3RlZWxfU2hpZWxkcz9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Steel Shields</span> from Eartheart.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Three_Swords?veaction=edit&section=4\" aria-label=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Around this time, the road to Channathgate was the stalking ground of <a href=\"/wiki/Tandith_Tornears\" title=\"Tandith Tornears\">Tandith Tornears</a> and his band of brigands. The stretch of the Trader's Way that grazed the <a href=\"/wiki/Forest_of_Amtar\" title=\"Forest of Amtar\">Forest of Amtar</a> was particularly susceptible to ambushes from the trees. Forces from Three Swords hunted for the bandits for many years but never caught them. The authorities of Three Swords asked the <a href=\"/wiki/Dwarves\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dwarves\">dwarves</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/Great_Rift\" title=\"Great Rift\">Great Rift</a> for assistance, reasoning that a substantial portion of their imports and exports traveled along that road.<sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-97_6-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-97-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Three_Swords?veaction=edit&section=5\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Three_Swords?veaction=edit&section=6\" aria-label=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-FRCS-map-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCS-map_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCS-map_1-1\">1.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCS-map_1-2\">1.2</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Map included in&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/Ed_Greenwood\" title=\"Ed Greenwood\">Ed Greenwood</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Sean_K._Reynolds\" title=\"Sean K. Reynolds\">Sean K. Reynolds</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Skip_Williams\" title=\"Skip Williams\">Skip Williams</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Rob_Heinsoo\" title=\"Rob Heinsoo\">Rob Heinsoo</a>&#160;(June 2001). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Forgotten_Realms_Campaign_Setting_3rd_edition\" title=\"Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting 3rd edition\">Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting 3rd edition</a></i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>). ISBN&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-7869-1836-5\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-7869-1836-5\">0-7869-1836-5</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-ESA-66-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-ESA-66_2-0\">2.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-ESA-66_2-1\">2.1</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ed_Greenwood\" title=\"Ed Gree